From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:56:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Map DOM selections and carets onto text layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Script-made selections never painted: the pointer-drag path fills
TextSelection with (inline root, layout byte) pairs that DOM code had no
way to produce. Bridge it:

- TextLayout records (text node id, byte range) per pushed text
  node, measured around each push via parley current_text_len:
  approximate under whitespace collapse, exact in the common
  one-text-node-per-commit case.
- set_dom_selection resolves DOM boundary points: text nodes map
  through the recorded range (UTF-16→UTF-8 against the original
  data, clamped into the range so collapse/transform/injected bidi
  controls can never point outside the node); element boundaries
  descend to the nearest text position through flat children so
  shadow content is reachable. Inline roots are found via the
  layout_parent chain; anonymous blocks never appear in the DOM
  parent chain.
- Feeds the same TextSelection the pointer path fills, so the
  existing highlight paint (multi-root ranges included) works
  unchanged.

The reverse of resolve_text_boundary, for the mousedown caret-placement
default action and drag-selection: find_text_position returns the inline
root plus a layout-byte offset, which Selection.collapse cannot consume.
Map the byte through the node_ranges table to the owning text node and
convert the layout slice to UTF-16 units, clamped into the node (layout
bytes shift under collapse/transform; the same approximation as the
forward direction).
